# Main flows

## Side navigation scrolls to sections
- Start: index.html
- Steps: click About, Experience, Education, Skills, Tech Stack, Dissertation, Projects, Interests in the side nav
- Expect: page scrolls to each section; active link highlighted

## Dissertation "Full summary" link
- Start: index.html#projects
- Steps: click "Full summary" in the CCIM card
- Expect: scrolls to Dissertation section

## Mobile nav
- Start: index.html at 375px
- Steps: tap hamburger, tap Projects
- Expect: menu opens, scrolls to Projects

## CV buttons in About
- Start: index.html#about
- Expect: CV PDF links resolve

# Requested change checks
- Each of the 11 documented projects has a linked title and a "Read the case study" link in index.html#projects
- Each link opens projects/<slug>.html with: title, context, contribution, key decisions with trade-offs, results, limitations, tags, and an evidence note
- Source galleries are present where suitable images exist; do not fabricate screenshots for text-only projects
- C# booking API and Vector Rally have links to the user-supplied GitHub repositories
- Project page side nav links back to index sections; "Back to projects" returns to index.html#projects
- Gallery images load (no 404), open enlarged on click, close with Esc / close button
- Previous/next project links work
- No console errors on any page; layout fine at 375px and 1280px
- Raw reports, lab credentials, flags, notebooks and build tools must not ship in the preview
- n8n and SOAP entries stay as summaries without a case-study link
- Open a project directly, use the browser Back button, and resize desktop to mobile and back
- At 200% equivalent zoom, content and navigation remain usable
